    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "as noted by Fisher (1941) and Kempthorne (1957). This general definition for the additive genetic variance holds for both randomly and nonrandomly mating populations. In the latter case, it reduces to",
      "source_page": 93,
      "printed_page": 73,
