      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "a9e6b0ef12d30ebf97061013cf5e14a25b879a2e08dae22d23f913059f26c900"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Finally, we consider the general definition of the breeding value ( $ A_{ij} $) under random mating. Parents with genotype $ B_{i}B_{j} $ transmit alleles i and j with equal frequency, and the expected additive effect of the allele contributed by their mates is equal to zero. Thus, the expected deviation of the mean phenotype of offspring of genotype $ B_{i}B_{j} $ from the population mean is",
      "source_page": 94,
      "printed_page": 74,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter4:p028:b3"
