    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Thus, the genotypic value at any locus can be decomposed into four quantities: the mean genotypic value for the population, the additive effects of the two genes (whose sum is the breeding value), and a dominance deviation due to the interaction between the genes. Since $ \\mu_{G} $ is a constant, and A and $ \\delta $ are (by the properties of least-squares regression) uncorrelated, it follows from Equation 4.26 that the genetic variance can be represented as",
