    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "This is a completely general definition, applying even to the case of nonrandom mating (although as noted above, the definitions of the $ \\alpha_{i} $ and $ \\delta_{ij} $ change with the degree of inbreeding). For the special case of random mating, $ \\alpha_{i} $ and $ \\alpha_{j} $ are uncorrelated, and",
