    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Comparing this with Equation 4.9, we find that $ \\sigma_{A}^{2} $ has a very specific and useful meaning. Under random mating, the additive genetic variance is equivalent to the variance of breeding values of individuals in the population.",
      "source_page": 94,
      "printed_page": 74,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter4:p028:b15"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        159.0,
